    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-4912",
      "problem": "Find a Cartesian equation of the line shown in the figure below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14117608/assets/792bf09ff2546903b863a879a2518c42bbd30fdfce652bd4e22b1ad19aefc7c9.png)",
      "worked_solution": "We know that the line passes through the points ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14117608/assets/aa4328c3ce96a1b9871e71f5cc27e255e47d186fe5848ea0f7d43b324d41a2d6.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14117608/assets/9a6a4549ad0127d861d9a5c0a1ceff0b41b7c06b648a327779f31b325ea5800e.svg) Now, we need to find a vector parallel to the given line. Let's consider the vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14117608/assets/e6db167bc32b19da05d87b24e9b910b80d32a1ef9e5965ab4cb5217a1fac4730.svg) which is given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14117608/assets/e17614c58be91b6165e40be1c489685e14898756db2d6a41bf80b638e666fc51.svg)\n\nUsing the point ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14117608/assets/1aaddf0d4be4d873ff6c0600b0b239e0565a05ca8daaff7ca92bd5c70bebcf03.svg) and the vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14117608/assets/e6db167bc32b19da05d87b24e9b910b80d32a1ef9e5965ab4cb5217a1fac4730.svg), we have that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the given line is given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14117608/assets/8df9f1471a16c7b99e55290a41fe97641d62cef3bf5ba0e57e7fe6c029e98807.svg)\nor equivalently\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14117608/assets/9e688c295265c270ba7e1f66fc13ceebe9f6385ea45000c6f42c204d3fb6ba50.svg)\n\nBut the above equation is problematic because ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14117608/assets/7435bec0e47e7cfafdcbdbf0763b77d55a16344504663512cbbcf8b75a50381f.svg) involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, in our line, the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14117608/assets/9032cb23a878659e74b670d3779a8cd4793b28af921eab1a6b3f2041a815e03b.svg) component always maintains the constant value ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14117608/assets/efcfb7a56c85727ded8a9d5c9bd75fd79ac0bc20ba202c2da6aaca3c4e3ba503.svg) For example, our two points ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14117608/assets/aa4328c3ce96a1b9871e71f5cc27e255e47d186fe5848ea0f7d43b324d41a2d6.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14117608/assets/dee63698dc962e270612a470eb5e1eb23ffcbd72c8f9d787bc7eb927ff05f1c6.svg) both have ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14117608/assets/9032cb23a878659e74b670d3779a8cd4793b28af921eab1a6b3f2041a815e03b.svg)-coordinates of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14117608/assets/efcfb7a56c85727ded8a9d5c9bd75fd79ac0bc20ba202c2da6aaca3c4e3ba503.svg)\n\nSo, in the Cartesian equation, we remove the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14117608/assets/7435bec0e47e7cfafdcbdbf0763b77d55a16344504663512cbbcf8b75a50381f.svg) part and instead write ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14117608/assets/6be447d259b9b63c2cdd7adc4107d7c96ed4df1730890fc1bb5ce7cd585b8ea6.svg) as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14117608/assets/92f849bc9c2fc37e54e4ecf4901b06624536d835db97d31f94ab77573d6e401b.svg)",
